    "notes": "Two DGX Spark GB10 (spark2 head, spark3 worker), tensor-parallel 2 over the QSFP/RoCE fabric on 10.99.23.0/24, Ray as the distributed executor. This checkpoint is 172.8 GiB of weights and does NOT fit one 128 GB box, which is the reason for the 2-node configuration. Both nodes were drained from their production cluster for the run and their GPU clocks explicitly unlocked (a drained node loses the gateway's clock governor and otherwise idles at ~600 MHz of a 3003 MHz ceiling). cluster-tts was left running on both nodes and holds roughly 20 GiB; that is why gpu-memory-utilization is 0.80 and not the 0.84 the recipe documents - at 0.84 startup fails outright with 'Free memory on device cuda:0 (101.27/121.69 GiB) is less than desired GPU memory utilization (0.84, 102.22 GiB)'. Nothing else was on either GPU. max-model-len is 32768 rather than the model's native 262144, with max-num-batched-tokens 2048 and --enforce-eager. This is deliberate and is the only configuration known to start: launching at native context wedged both boxes, because a post-load profiling pass allocates a dummy forward outside vLLM's own budget and --kv-cache-memory does not bound it. Do not read these numbers as a 262144-context result."
